# Accepted findings of "trivy config" (make security). Every entry MUST have a justification.

# KSV-0048: ClusterRole can delete pods.
# Accepted: deleting pods with errors is the purpose of the watchdog. The ClusterRole only
# grants get/list/watch/delete on pods and get/list on namespaces (least privilege).
KSV-0048

# KSV-0110: workload in the "default" namespace.
# Accepted: false positive of the static render. The chart is installed in the namespace
# chosen by the user (--namespace), the documentation recommends a dedicated namespace.
KSV-0110

# KSV-0125: image from an "untrusted" registry (docker.io).
# Accepted: the registry allowlist is organization specific. Users can mirror the image and
# change image.repository. The image tag is pinned.
KSV-0125

# KSV-0036: service account token mounted.
# Accepted: the watchdog needs the token to call the Kubernetes API. The pod sets
# automountServiceAccountToken=false and mounts a short-lived projected token explicitly
# (volume kube-api-access). The check reads the field from Deployment.spec instead of the
# pod template, so it always flags the explicit mount.
KSV-0036
